    "last_attempts_log": [
      {
        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 46.731,
        "asr_text": "At the end of a taxi ride or a meal, the payment screen asks one small question: How much would you like to tip? But the screen usually gives an answer first. It shows a few suggested percentages. The first choices may be higher than the amount you plan to give. That first number can change the whole decision. A 2014 study looked at more than 13 million credit card taxi payments in New York City. The researchers found a useful natural test. For fares just below $15 and just above $15, the suggested tip menu changed suddenly. The rides were almost the same price, but some passengers saw a different menu.",
