        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 32.761,
        "asr_text": "Passengers who saw higher suggested rates left more money. This suggests that the number on the screen can become a starting point. People may begin with that number instead of their own first idea. But there was a catch. When the suggested tip was too high, some customers did not simply choose a smaller amount. They chose zero. So a high default can raise the tip from some customers, but it can also push other customers away from tipping by card completely.",
