        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 33.491,
        "asr_text": "In the United States, restaurant tipping rose from about 10 to 15 percent in the early 1970s to about 20 percent in the late 1990s, according to one policy brief. Digital payment screens can now show tips as high as 35 percent. One expert argues that this changes the feeling of the moment. With a cash tip jar, the choice could be more private. With a screen held by an employee, the customer may feel watched. He calls this pressure tipping.",
