        "asr_text": "A 2026 survey found that 78% of respondents said tipping had become unreasonable; 44% said they were tipping less than the year before. Among consumers prompted by a digital screen to tip, the share who felt they had to leave a tip fell from 66% in September 2025 to 59% in 2026, and 36% said they chose a custom amount instead of a suggested rate. These are survey answers, not proof that the screen caused the change, but they suggest that many customers are increasingly pushing back against digital prompts to tip.",
